-We ran feature and head-path ablations and HF-only controls on the nine molecular and materials pools under the main protocol. They used 40 seeds, $B = 30$, and the same initial designs, fidelity schedule and greedy policy. The ablations change only the BLR head's input. We replaced the learned representation $\varphi^{(L)}$ with second-hidden-layer features from an untrained network of the same architecture. We also reduced the head to the scalar LF prediction. Separate ablations removed the LF prediction as an additive offset, a regression input or both. An HF-only network of the same architecture and training length was fitted to HF observations alone, with the same head. The HF-only controls started from the same two initial HF points and spent the whole budget on HF evaluations. These were SFGP with EI and uniformly random HF sampling. SFGP used BoTorch \texttt{SingleTaskGP} with a Mat\'{e}rn-5/2 kernel and library defaults. For each HF query, pick logs recorded the candidate, its LF-proxy rank and whether it had already been evaluated at LF. Supplementary Note~\ref{suppnote:controls} gives definitions and values.
+We ran feature and head-path ablations and HF-only controls on the nine molecular and materials pools under the main protocol. They used 40 seeds, $B = 30$, and the same initial designs, fidelity schedule and greedy policy. The ablations changed only the BLR head's input. We replaced the learned representation $\varphi^{(L)}$ with second-hidden-layer features from an untrained network of the same architecture. We also reduced the head to the scalar LF prediction. Separate ablations removed the LF prediction as an additive offset, a regression input or both. An HF-only network of the same architecture and training length was fitted to HF observations alone, with the same head. The HF-only controls started from the same two initial HF points and spent the whole budget on HF evaluations. These were SFGP with EI and uniformly random HF sampling. SFGP used BoTorch \texttt{SingleTaskGP} with a Mat\'{e}rn-5/2 kernel and library defaults. For each HF query, pick logs recorded the candidate, its LF-proxy rank and whether it had already been evaluated at LF. Supplementary Note~\ref{suppnote:controls} gives definitions and values.
 
